# Pinned external SOURCE BYTES for the reconstructed historical backtest
# (scripts/backtest). Tens of megabytes of third-party CSVs, deliberately not
# in git. They are NOT reproducible on demand: nine of the ten sources are
# nflverse release assets that are REPLACED IN PLACE, so a later fetch of the
# same URL can legitimately return different bytes. Only games.csv is
# content-addressed (commit + git blob). The recorded SHA-256s therefore PROVE
# that a copy is the pinned one; they cannot RECREATE it. Preserving
# backtest-data/sources/ out of band - an archived copy retained until the
# study publishes - is a REQUIREMENT, not a convenience.
#
# Everything DERIVED from those bytes is committed, because the
# preregistration is sealed against it: the provenance record below,
# backtest-data/observed-hosts.json, and backtest-data/inspection/.
backtest-data/sources/*
!backtest-data/sources/provenance.json

# The agent memory index is deliberately UNTRACKED: it auto-loads into an
# agent context from inside any clone, which defeated the review independence
# bar (round-2 disclosure). It stays local, like the hand-delivered review
# documents. docs/agents/* remains tracked - reference-only, never auto-loaded.
CLAUDE.md
